## How to act on this report

This report observes friction across recent Claude Code sessions and surfaces
commands that consistently produce high human-intervention rates, blocked
signals (`BLOCKED`, `redo`, `wrong`, etc. in user text), or run repeatedly
within the same session.

Harness does NOT auto-edit skill bodies. To address a hotspot:

1. Read the skill source for the flagged command under `src/harness/templates/base/skills/<command>/`.
2. Inspect the Step 0 context-load (preconditions too strict? missing input?).
3. Inspect the rubric / template body for ambiguity.
4. Inspect the final-summary verdict-mapping for unclear next-step instructions.
5. Edit the skill body, regenerate the harness (`harness generate`), and re-run
   the affected scenario. Re-run `harness tune` after a few sessions to verify
   the friction score dropped.

**Caveat:** small sample sizes (≤ 3 sessions) produce noisy metrics. Re-run
`harness tune --last 10` once enough session data accumulates.
